{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Archetype and Iowa fit my interest in forceful riffs and aggressive vocals, reflected in my listening to In Flames and Advance And Vanquish.",
    "Hybrid Theory and Toxicity offer memorable hooks alongside intensity; that combination connects with what appeals to me in Chuck and Ten Thousand Fists. Toxicity's unusual rhythms also fit my interest in 10.000 Days."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Music for Speeding interests me for its guitar playing, but I want vocals right now. Winterheart's Guild also has melodic appeal, though prominent keyboards are less appealing today.",
    "I passed on Eclipse and Confession because I could not confidently identify the albums from their titles. That uncertainty does not mean I dislike their sound."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An interest in heavy guitars seems to have been treated as enough, even though the balance of vocals, riffs, and melody determines what I actually choose.",
    "My earlier melodic rock listening seems to carry too much weight for today's mood: Silence in Black & White has some appeal, but I currently want something heavier."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices of Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days make intense vocals, distinctive rhythms, and strong hooks especially relevant right now.",
    "There is a difference between music I might enjoy eventually and an album I would choose today: Cryptic Writings appeals to me, but Archetype and Toxicity feel like closer matches to my current mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my interest in heavy, melodic music, but sometimes overlook the vocal character, rhythmic interest, and immediate mood that make one album more compelling than another."
}"}
